The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (cipher->ctx != NULL) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx);
}
```
Reason:
The code attempts to access the `ctx` field of the `ssh_cipher_struct` without checking if it is defined, which only occurs when `HAVE_LIBCRYPTO` is enabled. This results in a build error when compiling with the gcrypt library, as the `ctx` field does not exist in that context.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef HAVE_LIBCRYPTO
if (cipher->ctx != NULL) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(cipher->ctx);
}
#endif
```
Reason:
The fix adds a conditional compilation check for `HAVE_LIBCRYPTO` around the access to `cipher->ctx`. This ensures that `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free` is only called when `ctx` is defined, preventing the build error when using the gcrypt library.

